## Why This Is Asked
This problem introduces a dynamic programming angle where subarrays are weighted by their block index. It tests the ability to transform interval sums into prefix sums, derive a two-dimensional DP over position and block count, and implement solution reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Prefix sums for O(1) interval sum computation
- 2D DP over position and block count
- Solution reconstruction via parent pointers
- Time complexity: O(n²k); Space complexity: O(nk)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxScorePartition(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const P = [0];
  for (let x of A) P.push(P[P.length-1] + x);
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => new Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const parent = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => new Array(k+1).fill(-1));

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    dp[i][1] = P[i];
  }

  for (let t = 2; t <= k; t++) {
    for (let i = t; i <= n; i++) {
      for (let p = t-1; p < i; p++) {
        const score = dp[p][t-1] + (P[i] - P[p]) * t;
        if (score > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = score;
          parent[i][t] = p;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct partitions
  const partitions = [];
  let end = n;
  for (let t = k; t >= 1; t--) {
    const start = parent[end][t];
    partitions.unshift([start+1, end]);
    end = start;
  }

  return { maxScore: dp[n][k], partitions };
}
```

## Why This Question Is Asked

This problem tests dynamic programming with turn constraints on grid paths, requiring careful state design and path reconstruction. It evaluates understanding of edge case handling and performance optimization for large inputs.

## Key Concepts

- **4D DP state**: position (i, j), turn count (t), and ending direction (d)
- **Two transition types**: continuing in the same direction versus making a turn
- **Path reconstruction**: using parent pointers or backtracking to retrieve the actual path
- **Time and space trade-offs**: consider optimization for large grids

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxPathWithKTurns(M, k) {
  const n = M.length;
  const m = M[0].length;
  const dp = Array(n).fill(null).map(() =>
    Array(m).fill(null).map(() =>
      Array(k + 1).fill(null).map(() => [-1, -1])
    )
  );

  dp[0][0][0][0] = dp[0][0][0][1] = M[0][0];

  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    for (let j = 0; j < m; j++) {
      for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
        for (let d = 0; d < 2; d++) {
          if (dp[i][j][t][d] < 0) continue;

          if (i + 1 < n) {
            const newD = 1;
            const newT = d === newD ? t : t + 1;
            if (newT <= k) {
              dp[i + 1][j][newT][newD] = Math.max(
                dp[i + 1][j][newT][newD],
                dp[i][j][t][d] + M[i + 1][j]
              );
            }
          }

          if (j + 1 < m) {
            const newD = 0;
            const newT = d === newD ? t : t + 1;
            if (newT <= k) {
              dp[i][j + 1][newT][newD] = Math.max(
                dp[i][j + 1][newT][newD],
                dp[i][j][t][d] + M[i][j + 1]
              );
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }

  return Math.max(dp[n - 1][m - 1][k][0], dp[n - 1][m - 1][k][1]);
}
```

## Complexity

- **Time**: O(n × m × k)
- **Space**: O(n × m × k)

